    "content": "The United States military operates by far the largest fleet of C-130 Hercules aircraft globally, with an estimated total inventory of around 460 to nearly 600 aircraft across all variants (C-130H/J, MC-130, KC-130, HC-130). The Air Force holds the majority, followed by significant numbers in the Marine Corps and Navy. Key Breakdown of US C-130 Holdings: US Air Force: Approximately 460 aircraft (including Active, Reserve, and Air National Guard). US Marine Corps: Around 74 KC-130J aerial tankers. US Navy: Approximately 35 Super Hercules (including for TACAMO and Blue Angels). US Coast Guard: Around 25 HC-130J/H aircraft. The US is currently transitioning towards a fully modernized fleet centered on the Lockheed Martin C-130J Super Hercules, having taken delivery of over 77 of the new J-variants to date.",
